The primary drivers of the $85 million decrease in Cost of revenue, net and the $43 million decrease in gross loss and the increase in gross margins for the three months ended September 27, 2026 compared to the three months ended September 28, 2025 included the following:

• Lower revenues and unfavorable changes in overall product mix as discussed above;

• $8 million decrease in underutilization costs, reflecting stronger factory loadings as we align production with end market demand. We expect to continue to incur underutilization costs for as long as market demand for our products remains below our production capacity;

• $23 million decrease in write-downs related to customer-specific inventory we intend to scrap, partially attributable to our ongoing restructuring activities and gross increases of new reserves;

• $18 million decrease in restructuring and other closure-related costs, including accelerated depreciation and shutdown-related excess capacity charges.

